  "description": "VALSEI crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C54 H66 Mn4 N10 Nd4 O36,4(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Nd1B (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd2B (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Mn1B (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn2B (Mn) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.985-3.968 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.60-127.29°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Mn4Nd4O4(Me-sao)6(NO3)4(OMe)4(MeOH)2]·4MeOH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
